food antigen reactivity during infancy with concomitant expansion of responses to ubiquitous inhalant allergens</article-title><source>Pediatr Allergy Immunol</source><year>1995</year><volume>6</volume><fpage>85</fpage><lpage>90</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7581725</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b15"><label>15</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Szepfalusi</surname><given-names>Z</given-names></name><name><surname>Nentwich</surname><given-names>I</given-names></name><name><surname>Gerstmayr</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Prenatal allergen contact with milk proteins</article-title><source>Clin Exp Allergy</source><year>1997</year><volume>27</volume><fpage>28</fpage><lpage>35</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9117877</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b16"><label>16</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Van Duren-Schmidt</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Pichler</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Ebner</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Prenatal contact with inhalant allergens</article-title><source>Pediatr Res</source><year>1997</year><volume>41</volume><fpage>128</fpage><lpage>31</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8979301</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b17"><label>17</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Prescott</surname><given-names>SL</given-names></name><name><surname>Macaubas</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Holt</surname><given-names>BJ</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Transplacental priming of the human immune system to environmental allergens: universal skewing of initial T cell responses toward the Th2 cytokine profile</article-title><source>J Immunol</source><year>1998</year><volu